  - name: PATIENTSURVEY_DICT.Q53_HAS_PCP
    conditions:
      - questionText:
          EN: |
            <p>We will now ask questions about the patient’s access to a primary care provider.</p><p class="instruction">Note to enumerator [do not read]: This section is about the Patient’s Primary Care Utilization. Ask all questions in this section unless a skip rule applies. A primary care provider is your first contact healthcare provider (i.e., general practitioner doctor) for an undiagnosed concern or continuing care of varied medical conditions.</p><p>53. Do you have a primary care provider?</p>
          FIL: |
            <p>Magtatanong kami ngayon tungkol sa access ng pasyente sa isang primary care provider.</p><p class="instruction">Note to enumerator [do not read]: This section is about the Patient’s Primary Care Utilization. Ask all questions in this section unless a skip rule applies. A primary care provider is your first contact healthcare provider (i.e., general practitioner doctor) for an undiagnosed concern or continuing care of varied medical conditions.</p><p>53. Do you have a primary care provider?</p>
          BCL: |
            <p>provider Mahapot naman kami manungod sa access kan pasyente sa primary care</p><p class="instruction">Note to enumerator [do not read]: This section is about the Patient’s Primary Care Utilization. Ask all questions in this section unless a skip rule applies. A primary care provider is your first contact healthcare provider (i.e., general practitioner doctor) for an undiagnosed concern or continuing care of varied medical conditions.</p><p>53. Do you have a primary care provider?</p>
          BIS: |
            <p>provider Mangutana na usab kami bahin sa access sa pasyente sa usa ka primary care provider</p><p class="instruction">Note to enumerator [do not read]: This section is about the Patient’s Primary Care Utilization. Ask all questions in this section unless a skip rule applies. A primary care provider is your first contact healthcare provider (i.e., general practitioner doctor) for an undiagnosed concern or continuing care of varied medical conditions.</p><p>53. Do you have a primary care provider?</p>
          CEB: |
            <p>We will now ask questions about the patient’s access to a primary care provider.</p><p class="instruction">Note to enumerator [do not read]: This section is about the Patient’s Primary Care Utilization. Ask all questions in this section unless a skip rule applies. A primary care provider is your first contact healthcare provider (i.e., general practitioner doctor) for an undiagnosed concern or continuing care of varied medical conditions.</p><p>53. Do you have a primary care provider?</p>
          WAR: |
            <p>provider Magpapakiana kami yana mahitungod han pag-access han pasyente ha usa nga panguna nga parag-ataman</p><p class="instruction">Note to enumerator [do not read]: This section is about the Patient’s Primary Care Utilization. Ask all questions in this section unless a skip rule applies. A primary care provider is your first contact healthcare provider (i.e., general practitioner doctor) for an undiagnosed concern or continuing care of varied medical conditions.</p><p>53. Do you have a primary care provider?</p>
          HIL: |
            <p>Karun mangayo kita sang mga pamangkot parte sa pag-access sang pasyente sa primary care provider</p><p class="instruction">Note to enumerator [do not read]: This section is about the Patient’s Primary Care Utilization. Ask all questions in this section unless a skip rule applies. A primary care provider is your first contact healthcare provider (i.e., general practitioner doctor) for an undiagnosed concern or continuing care of varied medical conditions.</p><p>53. Do you have a primary care provider?</p>
          ILO: |
            <p>We will now ask questions about the patient’s access to a primary care provider.</p><p class="instruction">Note to enumerator [do not read]: This section is about the Patient’s Primary Care Utilization. Ask all questions in this section unless a skip rule applies. A primary care provider is your first contact healthcare provider (i.e., general practitioner doctor) for an undiagnosed concern or continuing care of varied medical conditions.</p><p>53. Do you have a primary care provider?</p>
  - name: PATIENTSURVEY_DICT.Q54_PCP_TYPE
    conditions:
      - questionText:
          EN: |
            <p>54. Who is your main primary care provider?</p>
          FIL: |
            <p>Ano ang iyong main primary care provider?</p>
          BCL: |
            <p>Siisay an saimong pinaka primary care provider?</p>
          BIS: |
            <p>Kinsa ang imong pangunahing primary care provider?</p>
          CEB: |
            <p>Kinsa ang imong nag-unang primary care provider?</p>
          WAR: |
            <p>Hin-o an imo panguna nga parag-ataman?</p>
          HIL: |
            <p>Sino ang imo pangunang primary care nga tagahatag sang serbisyo?</p>
          ILO: |
            <p>Siasino ti kangrunaan a mangipapaay iti panangaywanmo?</p>
